<title>DENMARK: Deutsche Finance increases 4% bond by 500 mln DKK.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Finance increases 4% bond by 500 mln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Deutsche Finance NV raised an existing four percent bond due 2002 by 500 million crowns to 2.250 billion crowns, arranger Sparekassen Nordjylland said on Wednesday in a statement distributed by Copenhagen Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Deutsche Finance said it, along with Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, had purchased the bonds for onward sale to investors.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969652</p>
